<p><strong>EDIT:</strong> Some of the information (but not all of it) in this comment is now outdated. Some of these gripes have been addressed in a revision. I am therefore changing my downvote to a novote.</p>
<hr />
<p>Hmm&#8230; The image's caption is incorrect, as it says it is included with every SCP-4986 instance; April 24th, 2003's entry clearly states no postage was included.</p>
<p>Additionally, the last entry is so poorly written that I initially thought it was vandalism.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;See&nbsp;what&nbsp;I&nbsp;mean?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;See&nbsp;what&nbsp;I&nbsp;mean?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>██ Liters of blood with a radiation levels upwards of 1████ mSv</p>
</blockquote>
<ul>
<li>Why censor the units? You've been using them up until now. It looks like you didn't want to bother thinking up a realistic amount of either and just blackboxed them.</li>
<li>Liters should not be capitalized.</li>
<li>&quot;a radiation levels&quot;</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p>M██████████ in northern N██ ██████ coordinates 4█.█████ -7█.██████ -█.███████</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Dear God, just cut it. This last entry is so aggressively bad that it has retroactively soured the rest of the article.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Because of these reasons, I'm giving this a -1 without hesitation.</p>

